< Cut the Earth into two equal parts, as you would halve an orange. Of all the ways to make the cut, which leaves the most land on one side? A half is named by the point at the middle of its surface, its centre. The answer usually quoted is the half centred near Nantes, in the west of France. I worked it out from freely available data and got a half centred in the sea off Catalonia instead. It is very nearly a tie: there are two best places, one off Catalonia and one in Brittany, beside Nantes; the half centred on either holds about 81% of the world's land, and the first wins by about the area of Estonia. It turned out that my answer had been in print since 2003, and I had not known it. Further down, the same question is asked about people and about woodpeckers.
